    [
     1,
     "<div>The line segments missing from the graph indicate that there are no individuals with the double-recombinant (AA,BB) and (BB,AA) genotypes.</div><div>But I would expect that the output would have NA for those values, such as in the example below, where the (AA,BB) genotype is absent.</div><div><br></div><div>karl<br></div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">set.seed(20210729)</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">library(qtl)</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">data(fake.f2)</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">fake.f2 &lt;- sim.geno(fake.f2, n.draws=128, step=1)</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">(out_effplot &lt;- effectplot(fake.f2, mname1=&quot;1@5&quot;, mname2=&quot;1@7&quot;))<br>$Means<br>         1...@7.0.AA 1...@7.0.AB <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">1...@7.0.BB</a><br>1...@5.0.AA 21.44141 20.17869       NA<br>1...@5.0.AB 22.67253 24.56918 18.60580<br><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">1...@5.0.BB</a> 17.75186 22.19160 25.44724<br><br>$SEs<br>          1...@7.0.AA  1...@7.0.AB  <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">1...@7.0.BB</a><br>1...@5.0.AA 0.6455828 4.4105666        NA<br>1...@5.0.AB 5.4346461 0.5265628 9.3071026<br><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">1...@5.0.BB</a> 4.5490475 6.8012948 0.7549752<br></span><br></div>"
    ],
    [
